From 0639393e5098a2fcc7a3f7743105321310efd996 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 12:31:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arifi-sync: search anchors in SOURCE only, so the manifest
 cannot vouch for itself

The independent Fable 5.1 LOW check of the R6 registration commit (1391460a0) blocked on a
defect in the guard that commit was hardening: `_anchor_present` excluded only
`patches/series`, and `tools/arifi-sync/protected-wins.json` is TRACKED and lists every anchor
literal by construction. So for all 35 anchors the whole-tree grep had a guaranteed hit that was
not source, and `validate` could never report an anchor absent while its own manifest was
committed - which is always. Delete a protected mechanism from live code, keep the file, and the
gate stayed GREEN over a win that no longer existed. A record of the mechanism satisfying a check
meant for the mechanism, which is the same class as the `patches/series` hole R6 had just closed.

Reproduced on real fork content before the fix (`85-R6B-SELFHIT-PLANTED.txt`): in a
`git clone --shared` at 1391460a0, deleting the 4 source lines carrying `kernel_mul_mv_tq3_4s`
and the 1 carrying `tag:repack-carveout` left the old rule with NONE anchor problems, the only
remaining hit for each being `tools/arifi-sync/protected-wins.json`. Under this commit's rule the
same planted ref names both entries, and the unplanted tip stays clean.

`_anchor_present` now excludes four homes, each a record and never the mechanism, each with its
own reason in the docstring and in UPDATE-RUNBOOK 4.3:

  patches/series     the generated patch always carries the anchor text          (R6)
  tools/arifi-sync   the manifest, baseline and resolutions quote every anchor    (R6B, blocking)
  *.md               prose; no FNM_PATHNAME, so it matches Markdown at any depth  (R6B, note N2)
  docs               the non-Markdown record files under the root docs tree       (R6B, note N2)

CHECKED lossless (`81-R6B-anchor-exclusion-probe.txt`): all 35 current anchors still resolve in
code under all four exclusions, and every surviving hit is a source or build file.

The regression test commits `protected-wins.json` into the fixture repository first - the real
fork shape - then deletes the anchor from the source file while keeping the file, so only the
anchor half of validation can fire. That step is why the R6 test could not see this: `_write_manifest`
writes the JSON to disk and never `git add`s it, so in the old fixture the manifest was untracked
and `git grep <ref>` could not find it. The corpus never entered the shape the fork is always in
(GREEN-BUT-BLIND, LL-255). The test also asserts the manifest really is tracked, so a fixture that
stopped reproducing that shape fails loudly instead of passing for the wrong reason.

Planted-red, one exclusion group at a time (`83-R6B-PLANTED-RED.txt`), so RED names its own cause:
dropping `tools/arifi-sync` turns ONLY the new test red; dropping `docs` and `*.md` leaves
everything green (they close note N2, not the block); the pre-R6 no-exclusion rule turns the new
test AND the series test red. The R6 subtree, series-only-anchor and shares-a-prefix must-not-fire
tests are preserved and green in every variant.

Also closes checker record note N1: `powerinfer-windows-port-avx-cure` protects
`ggml/src/ggml-cpu/CMakeLists.txt` and anchors on `-mprefer-vector-width=128`, but the commit that
put that flag there is ef2ed94a03309dd3235e98fa962e212f01a191cf (`build: wire powerinfer lib +
AVX-spill cure into CMake [series 0004]`, CHECKED ancestor of this branch, CHECKED touches that
file), which was on neither `commit` nor `also_commits`. Added as an `also_commit` with the reason
recorded. Its trailer is build-system only, so it is not in the strict registration set and no
count moves. No measured claim on that entry, or any entry, is changed by this commit.

Preserved and re-verified after the change: 38 tests OK (was 37, +1); validate rc 0 with 17
entries / 33 protected paths / 35 anchors; discover --all rc 0 with strict set 0, 30 baseline rows,
11 discharged and the same 3 visibly owed; check --incoming upstream/master rc 1 with the same 10
collisions. The three still-owed rows (d0112ab49, f81c6dfdf, 159c3a21d) remain owed for the same
reason: they need a decode tok/s ON/OFF A/B on a discrete-GPU host on the streamed-expert path,
which this seat does not have.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
Measured-effect: correctness only, no throughput claim
Lane: lane-209
